    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Post-war quarterly data\"\n---\n\nTable 8 repeats the estimation on quarterly data from 1948 to 2015, so\nthat the result does not rest on the Great Depression years. With time\naggregation the decision frequency $h$ is the number of decisions in a\nquarter, chosen on the grid 1 to 4. Without it $h = 1$: the agent\ndecides once a quarter.\n\nThe quarterly panel follows the model's conventions. Prices and\ndividends are real. The quarterly dividend is the trailing four-quarter\nreal sum divided by four, the usual treatment of the seasonal and\npayment-timing noise in quarterly dividends, and the price-dividend\nratio is price over that one-quarter flow because the model's\ntime-aggregated moment sums dividends over one sampling interval. The\nmean log P/D therefore sits about $\\log 4$ above the annual one.\n\n::: {#908c70da .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code code-fold=\"true\"}\nfrom great_tables import GT\n\nfrom geap.lrr.estimation import estimate_bky, load_quarterly, table8_frame\n\nKIKU_GT = dict(table_background_color=\"transparent\", table_font_size=\"0.92rem\",\n               heading_title_font_size=\"1.05rem\", heading_subtitle_font_size=\"0.85rem\",\n               source_notes_font_size=\"0.8rem\", column_labels_font_weight=\"bold\",\n               data_row_padding=\"4px\")\n\n\ndef fmt_params(gt, tab):\n    \"\"\"Two decimals for the large parameters, four for the rest, scientific for sigma_w.\"\"\"\n    idx = {name: i for i, name in enumerate(tab[\"parameter\"])}\n    two = [idx[n] for n in (\"gamma\", \"psi\", \"phi_d\", \"phi_d_sigma\", \"h\", \"J\") if n in idx]\n    three = [idx[n] for n in (\"rho_d\", \"p\") if n in idx]\n    sci = [idx[n] for n in (\"sigma_w\",) if n in idx]\n    four = [i for i in range(len(tab)) if i not in two + three + sci]\n    num = [c for c in tab.columns if c != \"parameter\"]\n    return (\n        gt.fmt_number(columns=num, rows=four, decimals=4)\n        .fmt_number(columns=num, rows=two, decimals=2)\n        .fmt_number(columns=num, rows=three, decimals=3)\n        .fmt_scientific(columns=num, rows=sci, decimals=2)\n        .sub_missing(missing_text=\"\")\n    )\n\n\nquarterly = load_quarterly()\nprint(f\"n = {len(quarterly)} quarters, {quarterly['date'].dt.year.min()} to {quarterly['date'].dt.year.max()}\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\nn = 272 quarters, 1948 to 2015\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Table 8\n\n::: {#85ba8a74 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nta = estimate_bky(quarterly, n_starts=3)\nno_ta = estimate_bky(quarterly, h=1, n_starts=6)\ntab8 = table8_frame(ta, no_ta)\nfmt_params(\n    GT(tab8)\n    .tab_header(title=\"Table 8. Model estimates using post-war quarterly data\")\n    .tab_spanner(label=\"Time aggregation\", columns=[\"ta_hat\", \"ta_se\", \"ta_paper\", \"ta_paper_se\"])\n    .tab_spanner(label=\"No time aggregation\", columns=[\"nota_hat\", \"nota_se\", \"nota_paper\", \"nota_paper_se\"])\n    .cols_label(parameter=\"\", ta_hat=\"estimate\", ta_se=\"SE\", ta_paper=\"paper\", ta_paper_se=\"paper SE\",\n                nota_hat=\"estimate\", nota_se=\"SE\", nota_paper=\"paper\", nota_paper_se=\"paper SE\")\n    .tab_source_note(\"Parameters are per decision period. Paper: BKY (2016) Table 8.\"),\n    tab8,\n).tab_options(**KIKU_GT)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"fagrdsmgoc\" style=\"padding-left:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-top:10px;padding-bottom:10px;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:auto;width:auto;height:auto;\">\n<style>\n#fagrdsmgoc table {\n          font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Fira Sans', 'Droid Sans', Arial, sans-serif;\n          -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n          -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;\n        }\n\n#fagrdsmgoc thead, tbody, tfoot, tr, td, th { border-style: none; }\n tr { background-color: transparent; }\n#