 Yaron (2016),\nTable 8. The quarterly panel is rebuilt from the same CRSP, BLS, and\nBEA sources as the annual one. The paper does not say how it treats\nquarterly dividends; the trailing-sum flow used here matches the\nmodel's mean and volatility of the price-dividend ratio at the paper's\nprinted vector to within 0.03, and its dividend-growth autocorrelation\nof 0.32 sits next to the model's 0.29. The estimates do not reproduce\nthe paper's contrast. With time aggregation the grid lands on the\npaper's two decisions a quarter, but with a risk aversion above the\nprinted 7.45 and a rejected J-test. Without it the risk aversion sits\nnear the printed 8.66 and the J-test does not reject. `NUMBERS.md`\nlists the open caveats.\n:::\n\n",
